#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# is_key_member

#% text
# `is_key_member(a, k)` is `true` when the association `a` has the key `k`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `a` may also be a list of rules.

#% item
# A key is a whole key: `is_key_member(a, [x, y])` asks about the key `[x, y]`, not about a path.

#% item
# Anything else than an association or list of rules gives `false`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
is_key_member(assoc(a -> 1, b -> 2), a)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_key_member(assoc(a -> 1), c)
#% output
#= false

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
is_key_member([a -> 1, b -> 2], b)
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `is_key_free`, `key_exists`, `lookup`
